From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msi: Reject feature trees deeper than 16 levels at CostFinalize.

AI-assisted (Codex), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later.

Windows 10 x64/i686 depth measurement: Root->DeepRoot->N succeeds for
N=1..14 (3..16 levels). N=15 (17 levels) and all larger measured chains
fail1603 in CostFinalize; CostInitialize and FileCost succeed throughout.
The supplied Design MSI maximum depth7 does not reach this limit.

Extend the cycle validator's existing per-call parent index and colors to
compute depth once per node, reusing a completed ancestor's depth. Root
depth is one. O(features+child edges), no recursive walk or guessed bound.
CostInitialize still checks only cycles; CostFinalize imposes the measured
limit before recursive costing. Only msi.dll changes.

Apply after msi-reject-cyclic-feature-parents.patch. V15 tests add explicit
16/17-level assertions, using the same contained graph fixture as v14.
The separate UI request reset requires the measured ExecuteAction transfer
candidate. This depth patch itself does not implement the UI handoff.

--- a/dlls/msi/action.c
+++ b/dlls/msi/action.c
@@ -1384,13 +1384,14 @@
 }
 
 /* Validate parent cycles before the recursive costing helpers can run.
- * This is graph validity, not an assumed Windows feature-depth limit. */
-static UINT validate_feature_cycles( MSIPACKAGE *package )
+ * CostInitialize checks only cycles; CostFinalize additionally enforces the
+ * measured Windows limit of 16 levels, counting each root as level one. */
+static UINT validate_feature_graph( MSIPACKAGE *package, unsigned int max_depth )
 {
     struct feature_parent
     {
         struct feature_parent *parent;
-        unsigned int state;
+        unsigned int state, depth;
     } *nodes, *node, *next;
     unsigned int count = list_count( &package->features ), i = 0;
     MSIFEATURE *feature;
@@ -1404,13 +1405,18 @@
             nodes[child->feature->selection_index].parent = &nodes[feature->selection_index];
     for (i = 0; i < count; ++i)
     {
+        unsigned int depth = 0;
+
         node = &nodes[i];
-        while (node && !node->state) { node->state = 1; node = node->parent; }
+        while (node && !node->state) { node->state = 1; ++depth; node = node->parent; }
         if (node && node->state == 1) { free( nodes ); return ERROR_INSTALL_FAILURE; }
+        if (node) depth += node->depth;
+        if (max_depth && depth > max_depth) { free( nodes ); return ERROR_INSTALL_FAILURE; }
         node = &nodes[i];
         while (node && node->state == 1)
         {
             next = node->parent;
+            node->depth = depth--;
             node->state = 2;
             node = next;
         }
@@ -1429,7 +1435,7 @@
     load_all_folders( package );
     msi_load_all_components( package );
     msi_load_all_features( package );
-    if ((rc = validate_feature_cycles( package ))) return rc;
+    if ((rc = validate_feature_graph( package, 0 ))) return rc;
     load_all_files( package );
     load_all_patches( package );
     mark_patched_components( package );
@@ -2357,6 +2363,9 @@
     MSIQUERY *view;
     WCHAR *level, *primary_key, *primary_folder;
     UINT rc;
+
+    /* Windows accepts 16 feature levels, rejects the 17th at CostFinalize. */
+    if ((rc = validate_feature_graph( package, 16 ))) return rc;
 
     TRACE("Building directory properties\n");
     msi_resolve_target_folder( package, L"TARGETDIR", TRUE );
